ms. It also provides reagents and kits, including cFluor reagents that are fluorochrome conjugated antibodies used to identify cells of interest for analysis on its instruments. In addition, the company offers automated micro-sampling system and automated sample loader system, an automated loaders designed to integrate seamlessly into the Cytek aurora and northern lights systems; SpectroFlo software that provides intuitive workflow from quality control to data analysis for Cytek aurora, northern lights, and Cytek aurora evo systems; and customer support tools. Further, it provides conventional flow and image-based flow cytometry instrumentation and related products and services under the Amnis and Guava brand names. The company serves pharmaceutical and biopharma companies, academic research centers, and contract research organizations. It distributes its products through direct sales force and support organizations in North America, Europe, China, and the Asia-Pacific regions; and through distributors or sales agents in Europe, Latin America, and the Middle East countries. The company was formerly known as Cytoville, Inc. and changed its name to Cytek Biosciences, Inc. in August 2015. Cytek Biosciences, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Fremont, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Wenbin  Jiang Ph.D. | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 702 people. Revenue per employee of $287K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Cytek Biosciences, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $762M market cap on $201M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 57% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $9M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -13.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -85.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 2.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 8.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 73/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 181% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cytek Biosciences (CTKB) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/cytek-biosciences-ctkb-q3-2026-182930000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793903976.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cytek outlines $208M-$211M 2026 revenue range while postponing business unit rollout to 2027 (NASDAQ:CTKB)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666708-cytek-outlines-208m-211m-2026-revenue-range-while-postponing-business-unit-rollout-to-2027","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793890607.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","product"]},{"title":"Cytek Biosciences, Inc. (CTKB) Reports Q3 Loss, Tops Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023734/cytek-biosciences-inc-ctkb-reports-q3-loss-tops-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3023734","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793835905.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"